[0.108, "o", "\u001b[2;1H\u001b[;m Ready\u001b[;m             \u001b[4;2H\u001b[1m\u001b[;m# Computers\u001b[22m\u001b[;m       \u001b[6;2H\u001b[4m\u001b[;mTravel topics\u001b[24m\u001b[;m > \u001b[4m\u001b[;mPreparation\u001b[24m\u001b[;m > \u001b[4m\u001b[;mEquipment\u001b[24m\u001b[;m > Computers\u001b[9;2HA \u001b[1m\u001b[;mcomputer\u001b[22m\u001b[;m can be useful for leisure travellers, and indispensable for \u001b[4m\u001b[;mbusiness travellers\u001b[24m\u001b[;m and\u001b[10;2H\u001b[4m\u001b[;mdigital nomads\u001b[24m\u001b[;m. There are specific articles for \u001b[4m\u001b[;mInternet access\u001b[24m\u001b[;m and \u001b[4m\u001b[;mInternet telephony\u001b[24m\u001b[;m.\u001b[12;2H\u001b[1m\u001b[;m## Understand\u001b[14;2H\u001b[22m\u001b[;mAs of the 2020s, a \u001b[4m\u001b[;msmartphone\u001b[24m\u001b[;m has apps for most daily needs; see also \u001b[4m\u001b[;mSmartphone apps for\u001b[15;2Htravellers\u001b[24m\u001b[;m. Accessing maps and tickets on your smartphone is much easier than getting to a\u001b[16;2Hcomputer to see them. In some cases the smartphone apps are even better than the computer\u001b[17;2Hoptions.\u001b[19;2HA \u001b[1m\u001b[;mtablet\u001b[22m\u001b[;m computer is lighter and cheaper than a laptop, but is less versatile. These mainly run\u001b[20;2Hthe same apps as a phone but they are generally easier to use because the screen is larger and\u001b[21;2Hit is often easy to add an external keyboard and mouse.\u001b[23;2HA \u001b[1m\u001b[;mnetbook\u001b[22m\u001b[;m computer is another option lighter and cheaper but less versatile than a laptop. They\u001b[24;2Hare quite adequate for web browsing, blogging, office applications and connecting to remote\u001b[25;2Hservers, but usually not for demanding applications such as software development or intensive\u001b[26;2Hgaming. Most do not run Microsoft Windows; this is a problem for some users, but others see it\u001b[27;2Has a major advantage.\u001b[m\u001b[m\u001b[m\u001b[0m\u001b[?25l"]
